EDICT 0007: the renderer's pointers through long on LLP64

Category: 64-bit correctness, no change in results on LP64.
Nine sites build a pointer from an integer of type long or unsigned long: the cache alignment of the
stack arrays (finalverts, basespans, ledges, lsurfs, spans), the cached edge of a medge_t (r_edges plus a
byte offset, twice also compared as a difference) and the step of the light surface's destination row. long
is 32 bits on 64-bit Windows, so the pointer lost its upper half and the first frame with a screen wrote
through it. size_t has the pointer's width on LP64 and LLP64; on LP64 it has long's width too, so Linux builds
compute the same values. The casts that only test the low bits of an address (r_main.c, d_fill.c, d_scan.c,
common.c) are unchanged.

--- a/r_alias.c
+++ b/r_alias.c
@@ -710,7 +710,7 @@
 
